## What to deliver

Build and rig the foundry up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a heavy masonry works base, an overhead crane
arm off its top, and a loading piston in its flank. The required interface is the
two auto **`crane_swing`** and **`piston_bob`** joints that rock the crane arm fore
and aft and bob the piston down and up on their own, while the `base` stays fixed.
Produce **every** required part and joint; you may add your own extra parts,
joints, or auto-play clips on top, but do not drop or contradict the required
interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json`
are your finished submission.
